{"step_index":539,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T10:59:00Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-26T10:59:00Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-26T10:59:01Z\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\n#!/bin/sh\r\n# op-dbus-release: application\r\nexec 2>&1\r\nrm -f -- /run/opdbus/runit-ready/op-web\r\n\r\nwait_dep() {\r\n    sv start \"$1\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\r\n    i=0\r\n    until sv check \"$1\" >/dev/null 2>&1; do\r\n        i=$((i+1))\r\n        [ \"$i\" -ge 90 ] && { echo \"dependency $1 not ready after 90s\" >&2; exit 1; }\r\n        sleep 1\r\n    done\r\n}\r\n# Was `wait_dep ovsbr0-addr` until 2026-08-13. ovsbr0-addr's helper does not\r\n# exist and its run script has no `set -e`, so its only real effect was to\r\n# touch /run/opdbus/runit-ready/ovsbr0-addr — which this service and incusd\r\n# both gated on. Retiring it (3tched-network-install.sh) therefore took both\r\n# down. opdbus-rundirs is what actually creates the rundirs op-web needs.\r\nwait_dep opdbus-rundirs\r\n# The bridge owns CognitiveServer and its single-writer RocksDB. Web must\r\n# not start until the bridge has completed replay and opened its socket.\r\nwait_dep op-grpc-bridge\r\n\r\nset -a\r\n[ -r /etc/op-dbus/environment ] && . /etc/op-dbus/environment\r\nset +a\r\n\r\nexport OP_WEB_BIND_ADDR=\"${OP_WEB_BIND_ADDR:-10.0.0.2}\"\r\nexport PORT=\"${PORT:-8080}\"\r\nexport OP_WEB_STATIC_DIR=/usr/local/share/op-dbus/dashboard-release\r\nexport OP_DBUS_GRPC_ADDR=\"${OP_DBUS_GRPC_ADDR:-https://10.0.0.2:8090}\"\r\nexport OP_DBUS_GRPC_CA_FILE=\"${OP_DBUS_GRPC_CA_FILE:-/etc/op-dbus/tls/tonic-svc0-ca.crt}\"\r\n# Serve the existing private HTTP endpoint. The ready bridge above proves\r\n# its host-owned TLS door is bound; no decoy or tunnel daemon is a dependency.\r\nunset OP_WEB_TLS_BIND\r\n# Live subscribe is tonic-web on lungs (10.0.0.2:8090), not HTTP SSE.\r\n# OP_WEB_SSE_BRIDGE / OP_WEB_SSE_HYDRATE stay unset (off). Allowlist only\r\n# matters if an operator re-enables legacy hydrate.\r\n# Human browsers obtain OIA1 from the decoy's authenticated WireGuard pickup.\r\n# Host-local IP mappings do not prove a caller's identity, so no SID1 pickup\r\n# or HTTP admin grant is configured here.\r\nexport RUST_LOG=\"${RUST_LOG:-op_web=info,info}\"\r\n\r\n# NOTE the readiness token is written BEFORE the exec, so it asserts \"the run\r\n# script got this far\", not \"op-web-server is serving\". `check` is what closes\r\n# that gap — it tests the listener, not the token. Do not let anything gate on\r\n# the token alone.\r\n/usr/local/libexec/op-dbus/helpers/runit-ready-signal op-web\r\nexec /usr/local/libexec/op-dbus/bin/op-web-server\r\n"}
