{"step_index":556,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T11:02:57Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-26T11:02:57Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-26T11:02:57Z\nShowing lines 1-50 of 377\n1: ---\n2: name: json-render\n3: description: >-\n4:   Expert skill for building json-render.dev catalog components, page specs, and\n5:   generative UI across three repos: /srv/git/json-render (library source),\n6:   /srv/git/odbus (Rust backend + op-web Axum server), and\n7:   /srv/git/3tched.com (separate chatbot-rendered UI repository).\n8:   Covers the full stack: defineCatalog → Zod schema → React component →\n9:   pageSpec → NAV_MANIFEST → factory plugin wiring → sealed blob pipeline →\n10:   gallery/catalog promotion gate. Also covers the D-Bus plugin schema for\n11:   json-render and schema-renderer in op-plugins.\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # json-render Skill\n15: \n16: ## Local deployment policy — runit, not systemd\n17: \n18: The user-designated UI repository is `/srv/git/3tched.com`, separate\n19: from `/srv/git/odbus`. Inspect its actual catalog, registry and build/sync inputs;\n20: the reference layouts below do not establish its implemented components.\n21: `/srv/git/operation-dashboard-ui-07` and `crates/op-web/ui/` are retired UI paths.\n22: \n23: The host uses runit. Backend runtime actions go through the authenticated D-Bus\n24: plugin surface. Only for authorized operator service work use `sudo -n sv`\n25: (for example `sudo -n sv status op-web`); never use `systemctl`, its shim, s6 or\n26: service6. Edit versioned runit inputs, not `/run/runit/service`. Backend deployment\n27: is btrfs send/receive of an explicitly prepared filesystem snapshot; there is no\n28: deployment script. Never hand-copy binaries. Static UI synchronization does not itself\n29: require an op-web restart. Do not create a parallel frontend backend or expose\n30: broker credentials to the browser.\n31: \n32: EMQX is the retained vendor-binary-backed `emqx` D-Bus plugin, independent of\n33: retired Netmaker. Broker events may drive authorized live state updates while\n34: the chatbot generates schema-pinned layout patches. A generated mode, component\n35: or action never grants permissions: enforce verified session and project ACLs\n36: server-side, including on streamed updates and reconnects.\n37: \n38: ## Overview — Three Repos, One System\n39: \n40: ```\n41: /srv/git/json-render                   ← upstream library (source of truth for API)\n42: /srv/git/odbus                         ← Rust backend\n43:   crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/json_render.rs    D-Bus plugin schema\n44:   crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/schema_renderer.rs\n45:   crates/op-web/src/handlers/ui_model.rs                Axum gallery/catalog routes\n46: /srv/git/3tched.com        ← active UI target; paths below are layout examples\n47:   src/json-render/\n48:     catalog/catalog.ts                 defineCatalog (app catalog contract)\n49:     catalog/registry.tsx               defineRegistry (component implementations)\n50:     catalog/components/                React component render functions"}
{"step_index":557,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T11:02:57Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-26T11:02:57Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-26T11:02:57Z\nShowing lines 1-50 of 286\n1: ---\n2: name: svelte\n3: description: Svelte 5 renderer for json-render that turns JSON specs into Svelte component trees. Use when working with @json-render/svelte, building Svelte UIs from JSON, creating component catalogs, or rendering AI-generated specs.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # @json-render/svelte\n7: \n8: Svelte 5 renderer that converts json-render specs into Svelte component trees.\n9: \n10: ## Quick Start\n11: \n12: ```svelte\n13: <script lang=\"ts\">\n14:   import { Renderer, JsonUIProvider } from \"@json-render/svelte\";\n15:   import type { Spec } from \"@json-render/svelte\";\n16:   import Card from \"./components/Card.svelte\";\n17:   import Button from \"./components/Button.svelte\";\n18: \n19:   interface Props {\n20:     spec: Spec | null;\n21:   }\n22: \n23:   let { spec }: Props = $props();\n24:   const registry = { Card, Button };\n25: </script>\n26: \n27: <JsonUIProvider>\n28:   <Renderer {spec} {registry} />\n29: </JsonUIProvider>\n30: ```\n31: \n32: ## Creating a Catalog\n33: \n34: ```typescript\n35: import { defineCatalog } from \"@json-render/core\";\n36: import { schema } from \"@json-render/svelte\";\n37: import { z } from \"zod\";\n38: \n39: export const catalog = defineCatalog(schema, {\n40:   components: {\n41:     Button: {\n42:       props: z.object({\n43:         label: z.string(),\n44:         variant: z.enum([\"primary\", \"secondary\"]).nullable(),\n45:       }),\n46:       description: \"Clickable button\",\n47:     },\n48:     Card: {\n49:       props: z.object({ title: z.string() }),\n50:       description: \"Card container with title\","}
